+ * Vendored file, modified in place (not upstream ESP-ADF). Added
+ * `reuse_conn_same_host` to http_stream_cfg_t below, and the matching logic
+ * in http_stream.c's _http_load_uri()/_http_close(), to fix an audible ~2-3s
+ * silence gap on esp32_wifi_streamer every time a live HLS window is
+ * exhausted: re-fetching the manifest then the next segment forced two full
+ * back-to-back TCP+TLS handshakes to the SAME host, because _http_load_uri()
+ * unconditionally called esp_http_client_close() before every single
+ * request. See http_stream.c's matching "LOCAL PATCH" comment block for the
+ * full mechanism and why it's safe (opt-in, defaults to false/old behavior
+ * for every other caller in the esp-adf tree).
+ *
+ * If esp-adf is ever updated from upstream, this field and the matching
+ * http_stream.c changes need to be reapplied by hand - grep both files for
+ * "LOCAL PATCH" to find every touched spot. Original files backed up at
+ * ../../../backups_V1.0/esp-adf/components/audio_stream/ before this patch.
+ *
+ * 2026-08-22 (second patch, same day): reuse_conn_same_host above only
+ * shrank that gap (~1-2s measured) because it can't help at all across the
+ * one hop that matters most: the live manifest lives on a DIFFERENT host
+ * (itsliveradio.apple.com) than every media segment
+ * (liveradio.music.apple.com), so the manifest-refetch -> first-new-segment
+ * transition is a forced cross-host reconnect no same-host reuse check can
+ * skip. Fixing that for real needs the next window's track list to already
+ * be known BEFORE the current one runs out, fetched on a genuinely separate
+ * connection while http->client is still busy delivering the last known
+ * segment - not simply absorbed by a bigger ring buffer (the math: ~32KB/s
+ * stream needs ~100KB of buffer to hide a 3s stall, far past what this
+ * heap-constrained/no-PSRAM chip can spare - see esp32_wifi_streamer/main/
+ * app_config.h's RADIO_HTTP_BUFFER_BYTES history).
+ *
+ * Added below: http_stream_get_tracks_remaining() (how many tracks are left
+ * unplayed in the currently-resolved live playlist - the caller's trigger to
+ * start prefetching) and http_stream_playlist_insert_tracks() (hands a
+ * separately-fetched-and-parsed batch of new track URIs to this element,
+ * appended to the SAME queue http_playlist_auto_connect_next_track() already
+ * drains, so once they're in, the transition to them is indistinguishable
+ * from an ordinary same-window segment-to-segment hop - no FINISH_PLAYLIST
